{"name":"Berber","hex":"#d8cfb6","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Berber","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A member of a particular ethnic group indigenous to Western North Africa.","A kind of traditional rug manufactured by the Berber people."]},{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A group of closely related Afroasiatic languages spoken in northern Africa, particularly Morocco and Algeria."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Berber"}],"entries":[{"title":"Berbers","blocks":[{"text":"Berbers, also known as Amazighs or Imazighen, are an ethnic group indigenous to North Africa. They are primarily connected by their use of Berber languages, which are part of the Afroasiatic language family."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Berber_flag.svg/330px-Berber_flag.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Berbers"},{"title":"Berber languages","blocks":[{"text":"The Berber languages, also known as Amazigh or Tamazight, are a branch of the Afroasiatic language family. They comprise a group of closely related languages spoken by Berber communities, who are indigenous to North Africa. Historically, they have been written with the ancient Libyco-Berber script, which now exists in the form of Tifinagh. Today, they may also be written in the Berber Latin alphabet or the Arabic script, with Latin being the most widespread."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Map_of_Berber_Languages_2018.png/330px-Map_of_Berber_Languages_2018.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Berber_languages"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Hoggar_peinture_rupestre1.JPG/500px-Hoggar_peinture_rupestre1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedi